Short:        pi coding agent for the Amiga
Author:       spotUP
Uploader:     spotup@gmail.com (spotUP)
Type:         comm/misc
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0; m68k-020
Requires:     TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, Miami, AmiTCP), util/libs/AmiSSL-v5-OS3.lha for https
Distribution: Aminet

C:amiga-pi: pi (pi.dev, version 1.1.0), the coding agent. It reads, searches and edits files
and runs commands with the model of your choice (Anthropic, OpenAI and compatible servers,
Google, Azure, Bedrock) and your own key. Lua extensions, prompt templates, skills and MCP
servers work as in pi. It stands alone: it installs on a plain Workbench (AmigaOS 3.0 or
newer) and runs in the Shell window, in a line mode; in an UP-Term window
(comm/term/up-term.lha, optional) it gets the full-screen mode and keeps its data in
UP-Term:var.

Install: unpack, double-click Install. It makes ENVARC:amiga-pi if it is missing and never
overwrites settings.json, models.json or auth.json. Uninstall removes C:amiga-pi and keeps
ENVARC:amiga-pi.

